sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant View as Client Browser
    participant Ctrl as PaymentHistoryController
    participant Svc as ServicePayment
    participant Repo as RepositoryPaymentAPIProxy
    participant ApiCtrl as PaymentsController
    participant PayRepo as RepositoryPayment
    participant DB as AppDbContext

    User->>Ctrl: GET /PaymentHistory/Index

    alt User is NOT logged in
        Ctrl-->>View: Redirect to /Account/Login
        View-->>User: Displays Login page
    else User is logged in
        Note over Ctrl: RequireLogin check and set SessionContext UserId
        Ctrl->>Svc: GetFilteredPayments(Newest, ALL, empty search, page 1, size 10)

        Svc->>Repo: GetAllPayments()
        Repo->>ApiCtrl: HTTP GET api/payments/history
        ApiCtrl->>PayRepo: GetAllPayments()
        PayRepo->>DB: BuildPaymentQuery().ToListAsync()
        DB-->>PayRepo: List<HistoryPayment>
        PayRepo-->>ApiCtrl: List<HistoryPayment>
        ApiCtrl-->>Repo: JSON response
        Repo-->>Svc: List<HistoryPayment>

        Note over Svc: BuildMergedHistoryAsync
        Note over Svc: FilterPaymentsByCurrentUser
        Note over Svc: ApplyDtoFilters, ApplyDtoSorting, GetPagedResultDto

        Svc-->>Ctrl: PagedResult<PaymentDataTransferObject>
        Ctrl->>View: return View(result)
        Note over View: Renders dashboard components
        View-->>User: Displays Payment History dashboard
    end

    User->>View: Opens filters and clicks Apply
    View->>Ctrl: POST /PaymentHistory/Filter

    Note over Ctrl: RequireLogin check and set SessionContext UserId
    Ctrl->>Svc: GetFilteredPayments(filter, paymentMethod, searchQuery, pageNumber, pageSize)

    Svc->>Repo: GetAllPayments()
    Repo->>ApiCtrl: HTTP GET api/payments/history
    ApiCtrl->>PayRepo: GetAllPayments()
    PayRepo->>DB: BuildPaymentQuery().ToListAsync()
    DB-->>PayRepo: List<HistoryPayment>
    PayRepo-->>ApiCtrl: List<HistoryPayment>
    ApiCtrl-->>Repo: JSON response
    Repo-->>Svc: List<HistoryPayment>

    Note over Svc: Filter by current user
    Note over Svc: Filter by method, search and date
    Note over Svc: Sort and paginate result

    Svc-->>Ctrl: PagedResult<PaymentDataTransferObject>
    Ctrl->>Svc: CalculateTotalAmount(result.Items)
    Svc-->>Ctrl: totalAmount
    Ctrl-->>View: JSON { items, totalCount, totalPages, pageNumber, totalAmount }
    Note over View: jQuery updates dashboard without reload
    View-->>User: Displays filtered and sorted payments